 add('intervals','I',2,v,'Recover all four sample summaries',r'<p>An interval from a normal sample of size \('+str(n)+r'\) has endpoints \('+tex(lo)+','+tex(hi)+r'\). It was calculated with the stipulated critical value \('+str(c)+r'\). Treat these values as exact. Recover the sample mean, unbiased variance, sum and sum of squares.</p>',[f('mean','Sample mean',mean),f('variance','Unbiased variance',var),f('sum','Sum of observations',total),f('squares','Sum of squared observations',ss)],r'<p>Use the midpoint for the mean and half-width h for the margin. Then \(s^2=n(h/c)^2\), \(\sum x=n\bar x\) and \(\sum x^2=(n-1)s^2+n\bar x^2\).</p>',dict(kind='reverse',n=n,lower=str(lo),upper=str(hi),critical=str(c),expected=list(map(str,[mean,var,total,ss]))))
